diff --git a/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..953ade49827c59c33303504c9cec300fa4f06a7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+## Why
+
+The matcher can already return up to three reranker-selected candidates, but production JSON discards every selection except the primary `ld_product`; the rest is visible only in debug data. Real tender evidence and the experiment history indicate that more retrieval rewriting and automatic scope routing are saturated or unsafe, so the next bounded experiment should test whether already-supported ambiguity can be made useful without changing matching decisions.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an optional, production-safe structured candidate-set field that exposes the ordered reranker selections and their per-candidate evidence when the result is `MATCHED`.
+- Keep the existing top-level `status`, `score`, and `ld_product` payload fields unchanged, with the first selected candidate remaining the primary product.
+- Do not add a new terminal status, alter retrieval, candidate fusion, reranking prompts, selection limits, or automatically convert any request to `NOT_FOUND`.
+- Keep the candidate set absent or empty for `NOT_FOUND` and `RERANK_FAILED`; do not promote raw retrieval candidates into a user-facing candidate set.
+- Add focused matcher and serialization coverage for ordered selections, compatibility, and non-match/failure behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `uncertainty-preserving-result-set`: Exposes evidence-backed, ordered reranker selections as an optional candidate set while retaining the legacy primary-match contract.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected package code: `models.py`, `matcher.py`, and `serialization.py`.
+- Affected interface: JSON emitted by `scripts/match_batch.py`; the additive field is available even with `--no-debug` and must not change existing fields.
+- Affected tests: matcher and serialization unit tests with mocked reranker output.
+- No prompt/provider changes, catalog/index changes, dependencies, Qdrant migration, or index rebuild are required.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/specs/uncertainty-preserving-result-set/spec.md b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/specs/uncertainty-preserving-result-set/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..725b360115777a3b4f0b66729ecbb46331e8f56a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/v2-cycle-05-uncertainty-result-set/specs/uncertainty-preserving-result-set/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Purpose
+
+Expose reranker-supported alternatives so consumers can act on genuine matching ambiguity without changing the established primary-match outcome.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Matched responses expose an evidence-backed candidate set
+For every `MATCHED` response with one or more reranker selections, the production payload SHALL include a `candidate_set` array in the reranker selection order. Each entry SHALL identify the selected catalog product by `name` and `article` and SHALL include the reranker `confidence` and `reason`. The first entry SHALL identify the same product as the existing `ld_product` field.
+
+#### Scenario: Reranker selects multiple compatible products
+- **WHEN** the reranker returns `MATCHED` with two valid selected candidates
+- **THEN** the payload contains both candidates in reranker order, includes each selection's confidence and reason, and keeps `ld_product` equal to the first candidate
+
+#### Scenario: Reranker selects one product
+- **WHEN** the reranker returns `MATCHED` with one valid selected candidate
+- **THEN** the payload contains a one-entry `candidate_set` and preserves the existing `ld_product`, `status`, and `score` values
+
+### Requirement: Candidate-set exposure preserves non-match semantics and compatibility
+The candidate set SHALL be derived only from valid reranker selections. `NOT_FOUND` and `RERANK_FAILED` payloads SHALL expose an empty `candidate_set`; they SHALL NOT expose unselected retrieval candidates. Existing top-level `query`, `status`, `score`, and `ld_product` fields SHALL retain their current meaning and values, and disabling debug output SHALL NOT remove `candidate_set`.
+
+#### Scenario: No reranker-supported product exists
+- **WHEN** a result is `NOT_FOUND` or `RERANK_FAILED`
+- **THEN** the payload contains an empty `candidate_set`, preserves the current null `ld_product` behavior, and does not convert retrieved candidates into selections
+
+#### Scenario: Consumer requests no debug information
+- **WHEN** a matched response is serialized with debug output disabled
+- **THEN** the payload still contains the production candidate set and omits only the debug section

