@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+## 1. Production result-set projection
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add a focused public serialization projection for `SelectedMatch` that returns only `name`, `article`, `confidence`, and `reason`; verify it does not expose retrieval/debug-only fields.
+- [ ] 1.2 Add the always-present `candidate_set` field to serialized match results, populated in `MatchResult.selected` order and empty when there are no valid selections; verify the legacy `query`, `status`, `score`, and `ld_product` values remain unchanged.
+
+## 2. Focused behavioral coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add serialization tests for multi-selected and single-selected `MATCHED` results, verifying order, per-item confidence/reason, and equality of the first candidate-set product with `ld_product`.
+- [ ] 2.2 Add serialization tests for `NOT_FOUND` and `RERANK_FAILED`, verifying empty candidate sets, null primary products, and no promotion of retrieved candidates.
+- [ ] 2.3 Add a `include_debug=False` regression test verifying `candidate_set` remains available while the debug section is absent.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run `python -m pytest -q tests/test_serialization.py tests/test_matcher.py tests/test_reranker.py` and verify all focused result-contract tests pass.
+- [ ] 3.2 Run `python -m pytest -q` and verify the full deterministic suite passes; leave public/hidden evaluation, promotion, rollback, git actions, and index budgeting to the outer supervisor.

